 "steps": [
  {
   "caption": "f = AB + A′C with B = C = 1, so logically f = A + A′ = 1 whatever A does. A falls at t = 3; the inverter makes A′ rise one unit later, at t = 4.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "note",
     "set": {
      "text": "B = C = 1: f should stay 1"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "AB follows A and falls at t = 3; A′C follows A′ and rises only at t = 4. For one time unit both AND outputs are 0.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "l2",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "w2",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "l3",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "w3",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "So f = AB + A′C drops to 0 between t = 3 and t = 4: a static-1 hazard. On the map the two 1-cells m7 (A = 1) and m3 (A = 0) are adjacent but lie in different loops.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "l4",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "w4",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "pulse",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "note",
     "set": {
      "text": "glitch: 1 → 0 → 1 while A changes",
      "tone": "danger"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "Add the consensus term BC, the loop that contains both m3 and m7. With B = C = 1 it is 1 throughout, so f = AB + A′C + BC stays 1: the hazard is gone, at the cost of one more AND gate.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "l5",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "w5",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "l6",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "w6",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "note",
     "set": {
      "text": "add BC: every adjacent pair of 1s now shares a loop",
      "tone": "success"
     }
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
